respect.body:
Engage with respect, even when you disagree. The following are not allowed, in a post, a comment or a message:

– harassment: repeated or insistent messages, group mockery, intimidation, remarks meant to humiliate or isolate a person;
– insults and degrading remarks;
– hatred and discrimination on grounds of origin, ethnicity, province, nationality, language, religion, sex, sexual orientation, age, disability or opinion;
– threats, calls to violence and the glorification of violence.

If a person bothers you, you can block them from their profile: you will no longer see each other, and your links are broken. You can also mute them, hide a post or remove a comment left under one of yours.

A report of harassment receives a decision notified within 72 hours (Ordinance No. 0011/PR/2026, Article 24).

scams.body:
Do not offer a service that you do not provide, nor a job offer, housing or procedure that does not exist, and do not publish information that you know to be false. In particular, the following are prohibited:

– requests for money, advances or fees to obtain a job, housing, a visa, a residence permit or an appointment;
– fake fundraisers, miracle investments, pyramid schemes and promises of winnings;
– fake reviews and bought reviews;
– false information that can cause harm, for example about health, an administrative procedure or an election.

Be wary of anyone who pressures you to pay or to leave the network to continue the exchange. DIASPORA.GA collects no payment, membership is not paid for, and no consular procedure is handled on it. Contact goes through messaging: no address and no member’s number is published.

prohibited.body:
The following are not allowed:

– sexual or pornographic content;
– any sexual depiction of a minor, whatever the technique used, and any content harmful to a minor;
– sexual deepfakes of a person without their consent, and deepfakes that attribute to a person words or acts they did not say or do, such as to cause them serious harm;
– the glorification of terrorism, crimes and violence, and incitement to commit them;
– the promotion or sale of illegal products and services: narcotics, weapons, forged documents, medicines sold without authorisation, illegal border crossing;
– images of violence or suffering shown to shock;
– incitement to suicide or self-harm;
– malware and booby-trapped links;
– more broadly, any content contrary to Gabonese law or to the law of the country where you live.

If you publish an image, a sound or a video produced or altered by artificial intelligence that could pass for real, say so clearly.

Prohibited artificial intelligence content is removed within 24 hours of being reported, as is a deepfake reported by the person it depicts (Ordinance No. 0011/PR/2026, Articles 32 and 33). A report of content harmful to a minor receives a decision within 72 hours (Article 24). Such content may be passed to the authorities.

pages.body:
Whoever runs a page or a group is answerable for it. The managers of a page:

– keep it under the exact name of the organisation it presents, and are entitled to speak in its name;
– publish accurate information: activities, places, dates, prices, terms of an offer;
– ask no fee from a person who applies for a job offer;
– remove illegal content published on the page and respond to reports;
– do not leave the page abandoned: they put it to sleep or hand it over.

The Law makes the administrator of a page or group responsible for the illegal content that circulates on it (Ordinance No. 0011/PR/2026, Article 11).

measures.body:
After examination, the moderation team closes the report or takes a measure, proportionate to the seriousness of the facts, their repetition and their effects:

– removal of the content;
– a warning;
– mute, which prevents posting in DIASPORA.GA;
– suspension, which closes access to the network for a period;
– exclusion, which closes it with no end date.

A mute or a suspension lasts 365 days at most and ends by itself. Suspension and exclusion apply to the whole of ANTSIA, because the account is shared; “My data” stays open.

Some content is reviewed before it appears. No one rules on a case in which they are a party.

Each decision is reasoned. The person concerned finds it in “My data”, without the name of who reported or of who decided, and can contest it by a reasoned appeal. The appeal is examined by the network’s administration and then, on a second appeal, by the ANTSIA platform team, each time by a person other than the one who decided. No time limit is imposed for lodging an appeal.

You can also refer a complaint to the High Authority for Communication (Ordinance No. 0011/PR/2026, Article 38), or to a court. The publisher carries out the measures ordered by the courts: suspension of an account or of content, delisting, publication of a correction.
